      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The oldest church in Pennsylvania, Gloria Dei (Old Swedes') Church, was founded in 1677 and its current brick building dates to 1700.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://philadelphia.wiki/a/Queen_Village",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Sparks Shot Tower, a 142‑foot brick structure built in 1808, still stands as one of the few surviving shot towers in America.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://philadelphia.wiki/a/Queen_Village",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Queen Village’s streets trace back to the 1640s Swedish settlement, making it the oldest continuously inhabited European settlement in Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://philadelphia.wiki/a/Queen_Village",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s revitalization began in the 1970s when urban pioneers and gentrifiers restored historic buildings and opened new construction.",
